export anchor CockpitAvionicsStyle:
    number: 74
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Cockpit avionics
    idea: A light-mode flight deck where every number is an instrument in a screwed-down bezel, projects are vertical tape gauges and trouble lights up as an amber caution caption.
    base: light
    palette:
        deck: #dfe2dc, the page behind the panels
        bezel: #eef0eb, raised instrument housings and nav keys
        face: #fafbf7, dial faces, displays and fields
        ink: #15191c, text, needles, tape fill and the primary key
        dim: #4b534f, captions and meta
        selectedMagenta: #a1166f, tape bugs, log times, the week marker and focus
        green: #1b6a3a, the On track caption and normal arcs on dials
        cautionAmber: #f0b13a, caution fills with near-black text, never text itself
        warningRed: #b11f1a, the Behind caption with white text
        sky: #cfe2f1, the upper half of the attitude indicator
        ground: #e8d6b8, the lower half of the attitude indicator
    type:
        Two stacks. Captions use Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica
        Neue, Arial in bold caps tracked 0.14em at 11 to 12px. Readouts,
        times and the activity log use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas. The greeting is 26px bold condensed, readouts 22px bold
        mono in a small boxed window, tape percents 20px bold mono, project
        names 13px bold condensed and log lines 13px mono with bold magenta
        times.
    layout:
        A grey glareshield bar holds the brand with a small dial mark and
        the subtitle FLIGHT DECK, a row of square push keys for nav with a
        green lamp strip lit on Home, a monospace scratchpad search, a black
        New project key, an amber Notices 3 caution button and Pilot in
        command Mara Okafor. Below, a long bezel is the message line with
        the greeting, the date in mono caps and an amber caption reading
        Caution 4 tasks overdue. A row of five bezels follows, four round
        dials with a 270 degree tick arc, a coloured value arc, a needle and
        a boxed readout for the four summary numbers, the overdue dial with
        an amber caution band, and an attitude indicator whose horizon sits
        nose up for the week trend 73 against 59. The lower area has a wide
        Project systems bezel with six vertical tape gauges side by side,
        each with its percent above, a magenta bug at the fill level, name,
        team, tasks and due in mono, and a status caption under it. The
        right column stacks a Climb log bar chart on a display, last week as
        outlined bars and this week solid with a dashed magenta divider, and
        a Datalink messages log. At 375px the dials go two by two, the
        attitude indicator spans the row and the tapes go three across.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between bezels, 20px inside them and 10px between keys and tapes.
    density: Medium. Few large instruments with small captions, readouts carry the weight.
    corners: 14px on bezels, 6px on displays, 4px on keys and fields and 2px on captions.
    borders: A 1px grey rim on bezels and displays, 1px ink on dials and tapes, dashed rows in the log, and an 8px screw drawn in each bezel corner.
    shadows: Bezels are raised with a white top highlight, a 2px lip and a soft blur. Displays and fields are inset.
    icons:
        Instrument drawings only, dials with needles, tape gauges with a
        magenta bug and an attitude ball. Status captions pair the word with
        an open green circle for On track, a solid triangle on amber for At
        risk and a white square on red for Behind. Behind and At risk tapes
        also use striped fills.
    focus: A 2px magenta outline offset 2px with a soft 5px magenta halo at 18 percent.
    tone: Clipped checklist caps such as Caution 4 tasks overdue, Climb log, Datalink messages and 12 MIN.
